    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1829">

                <pb facs="1194" n="1078" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1078"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 816.001 Q4/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Salvador to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Salvador</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-09-23">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 23, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to
                    your excellency the autographic letter which Dr. Alfonso Quiñónez M., President
                    of Salvador, sends to His Excellency the President of the United States of
                    America, informing him of the fact that he has assumed the office of Chief
                    Executive of the Republic by virtue of the leave of absence granted by the
                    National Assembly to Mr. Carlos Meléndez.</p>
                <p>While requesting your excellency to be so kind as to deliver the said autograph
                    letter to His Excellency President Wilson,</p>
                <p>I take [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francisco Dueñas</hi></signed>.</closer>


                <xi:include href="d1829-a1.xml" xpointer="d1829-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
